 "text": "Hey there! How's your day been so far? It depends on how much you ride and the tire type. Generally, for civilian use, every two or three seasons is enough. Find a digital gauge and check one of the free rim spots. Tighten gently with a tube in, and stop if you feel resistance. Many people do, but it easy to overdo it and tear the tube. Take it off and let it dry first. Then go a bit lighter. Water causes tiny bubble where the tyre meets the rim, and that beats a standard tube.",
